  "text": "Beneath the lamps’ ethereal, pale light,\nHe walked the streets where shadows bite.\nEach footfall echoed, stark and clear,\nOn pavement cold, devoid of cheer.\n\nLike ghosts, the crowds drifted by,\nWith eyes cast down, averted eye.\nLost in their own deep, private spheres,\nHe felt the weight of solitude here.\n\nAmid the urban, heaving sea,\nHe stood alone, a mystery.\n\nThe animal known for its long neck is the **giraffe**."
